    "prompt": "Use the attached image as the BASE identity reference, not as a background. Preserve the same adult dockworker's face, natural human proportions, right-facing quiet pose, original painted2D rendering, lighting, broad construction-frame family and explicit living operator. Make its REINFORCED UPGRADE according to the following brief; pull back enough to give 10% transparent margin on EVERY side and complete the flagpole and both cargo claws with nothing clipped. No new unrelated subject or changed camera.\n\nCreate a single original 2D painted creature sprite master for Heroes of Might and Magic III, transparent background, full body and all equipment fully inside generous clear margin. Subject: Piltover Reinforced Dockyard Lifter, the advanced variant of the living crewed walking dockyard construction frame. ONE living adult dockworker must be clearly visible inside the open operator cage: face under a practical protective work helmet, shoulders, forearms using controls, brown leather safety harness. The human is not replaced by a robot head. Very substantial buttressed work feet, reinforced articulated load-bearing knees, broad shoulder/cage guards, protected hydraulic joint cylinders, robust counterweight and heavier steel/brass lifting jaws on two low articulated work arms. Well designed open-sided safety cage preserves a clear view of the operator; functional plating and load paths, no closed giant metal humanoid box. Aged bronze hinges, worn dark steel, limited ivory enamel guards, brown leather/timber details and a larger navy work pennant. On a credible broad front safety guard paint the documented Piltover regional crest: paired vertical central stem rising to an open circular upper ring around a small central orb, broad open lower horseshoe arc with gear-toothed outer flanks, warm gold on navy. Keep its real shape; not wings, not a generic cog, not Demacia.\nArt direction: the richly textured original 1999 Heroes III native creature rendering language in original hand-painted 2D, compact broad TWO-HEX silhouette, light from upper left, slightly elevated battlefield three-quarter view, body facing RIGHT while front/crew remain visible. This is an engineered upgrade to the same practical open walking frame: greater armor coverage, cage/shoulder breadth, protected joints, visible larger feet and stronger lifting jaws, not merely a recolor or extra logo. Subject about 120 native gameplay pixels high; operator remains recognizable. Stable holding stance, two planted feet on one ground plane, clamp arms balanced low. Transparent background, no floor, no shadow drawn outside character, no stage, no labels, no UI, no unrelated people. No 3D/Blender render look, glossy plastic, concept-art poster framing, anime, oversized modern science-fiction mech guns, Zaun chemicals, flight, resurrection, ethereal aura or copied HoMM3 monster. Restrained navy/bronze/steel materials and only tiny protected cool-blue power glass.\n",
